{"text": "France's longest land border isn't with Spain or Germany, it's with Brazil. Because way down in South America, French Guiana is still fully part of France, sharing a 730-kilometer jungle border with Brazil and making the European Union border South America. And Canada doesn't just border the United States. Way up in the freezing Arctic, Canada shares a land border with Denmark because in 2022, they finally split tiny Hans Island right down the middle. Down in Europe, Spain shares a 1.2-kilometer border with the United Kingdom at Gibraltar, and right across the water, Spain borders Morocco on a tiny rock connected by sand, creating the shortest land border on Earth at just 85 meters wide. In Southern Africa, four countries almost crash into a single point, leaving Botswana and Zambia a gap just 150 meters wide. So they had to build a curved bridge just to avoid touching Namibia and Zimbabwe. And if you think Norway is far from Asia, it's separated from North Korea by just one single country, Russia, which still isn't as wild as the fact that", "words": [{"text": "France's", "start": 0.12, "end": 0.56, "type": "word"}, {"text": "longest", "start": 0.74, "end": 1.1, "type": "word"}, {"text": "land", "start": 1.2, "end": 1.4, "type": "word"}, {"text": "border", "start": 1.48, "end": 1.76, "type": "word"}, {"text": "isn't", "start": 2.24, "end": 2.46, "type": "word"}, {"text": "with", "start": 2.5, "end": 2.6, "type": "word"}, {"text": "Spain", "start": 2.72, "end": 3.1, "type": "word"}, {"text": "or", "start": 3.34, "end": 3.44, "type": "word"}, {"text": "Germany,", "start": 3.56, "end": 3.98, "type": "word"}, {"text": "it's", "start": 4.48, "end": 4.64, "type": "word"}, {"text": "with", "start": 4.7, "end": 4.96, "type": "word"}, {"text": "Brazil.", "start": 5.38, "end": 6.02, "type": "word"}, {"text": "Because", "start": 6.52, "end": 6.9, "type": "word"}, {"text": "way", "start": 6.96, "end": 7.12, "type": "word"}, {"text": "down", "start": 7.16, "end": 7.34